<section style="padding:3rem 0;border-top:1px solid var(--color-border)"><div style="max-width:900px;margin:0 auto;padding:0 1.5rem"><h2 style="font-size:clamp(1.5rem,3vw,2rem);font-weight:600;color:var(--color-text);margin-bottom:1.5rem">Why Partner with SDF Clothing?</h2><p style="color:var(--color-text-muted);line-height:1.8;margin-bottom:1.5rem">Fabric sourcing runs through our own mill relationships rather than a trading company adding a markup between you and the mill. We test every incoming fabric lot for shrinkage, colorfastness, and pilling resistance before it reaches the cutting floor, catching problems before they reach your production run. GOTS, OEKO-TEX Standard 100, BSCI, WRAP, and ISO 9001 certification cover the facility.</p><p style="color:var(--color-text-muted);line-height:1.8;margin-bottom:1.5rem">Bangladesh's domestic textile mills supply roughly 85% of local knit fabric demand and around 40% of woven fabric demand, according to Bangladesh Textile Mills Association data — a backward linkage that shortens lead time on knit-heavy sourcing specifically. Minimum order is 300 pieces per style, with fabric sourcing, testing, sampling, and export documentation handled in-house.</p><p style="color:var(--color-text-muted);line-height:1.8;margin-bottom:1.5rem">Fabric-sourcing decisions carry Bangladesh's full trade position downstream into your finished garment cost: EU duty-free access under Everything But Arms through November 2029 despite LDC graduation in November 2026, and a 20% US tariff cap from late 2025 that keeps landed cost below Chinese-sourced fabric facing Section 301 duties.</p><p style="color:var(--color-text-muted);line-height:1.8;margin-bottom:2rem">Ready to start? <a href="/contact/" style="color:var(--color-primary)">Request a sample</a> or <a href="/contact/" style="color:var(--color-primary)">contact our team</a> for a detailed FOB quote within 48 hours.</p></div></section>
